It implements ADS, Beckhoff's Automation Device Specification, as Beckhoff
Automation GmbH & Co. KG documents it in the Beckhoff Information System,
and Secure ADS as Beckhoff's manual "TwinCAT 3 Secure ADS" describes it,
with what goes inside the TLS connection as described by the README of
https://github.com/kevinherron/beckhoff-secure-ads (MIT License,
Copyright (c) 2026 Kevin Herron). No text or code of those is included.

Finding devices and adding routes over UDP port 48899 follows the UDP code
of Beckhoff's own ADS library, https://github.com/Beckhoff/ADS (MIT
License; AdsLib/AdsLib.cpp, Copyright (c) 2021 - 2022 Beckhoff Automation
GmbH & Co. KG), which was read to write it. None of its code is included.

Deleting routes over UDP port 48899 follows Apache PLC4X's description of
ADS discovery, protocols/ads/src/main/resources/protocols/ads/
ads-discovery.mspec in https://github.com/apache/plc4x (Apache License 2.0,
The Apache Software Foundation), which was read to write it. None of its
text is included.

